{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The powered USB hub feels useful because my keyboard, card readers, and other desk accessories create a practical need for more organized connections and individual power switches.",
    "The memory card and reader fit my repeated use of removable storage and computer accessories, provided the card works with the device I intend to use."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks and smart plug do not support my current computer setup and maintenance tasks; owning electronics does not mean I am starting a streaming or Alexa project.",
    "The Ethernet and HDMI cables match things I use, but recent purchases already cover those needs, so another pack or a longer cable has no clear purpose today.",
    "The sport earbuds do not follow from my desk-oriented headphone use, and interest in storage alone does not give me a reason to install a 4TB internal drive."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched into interest in almost any electronic device.",
    "Previous cable and storage purchases seem to have been treated as reasons to buy more without considering whether I need a replacement, extra capacity, or a different connection."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases fit a practical desk and wired-network setup, where a useful next item should solve a remaining connection, organization, or maintenance need.",
    "Recently buying five Ethernet cables matters because it makes another cable pack less useful right now, even though it fits my interests.",
    "Storage format and device compatibility matter to me: removable memory with a reader serves a different purpose from a large internal SSD."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my computer-accessory needs but missed which purchases would fill a current gap rather than repeat a solved need or introduce an unrelated project."
}"}
